Examinations after admission:
CBC: WBC 3.9×10^9/L, N 72.4%, Ly 0.7×10^9/L, Hb 137 g/L, PLT 310×10^9/L.
Blood chemistry: ALB 35 g/L, Na+ 127 mmol/L;
Stool routine: fungus (+), pus cells (+);
TORCH: rubella virus IgG (+), CMV-IgG (+), HSV-IgG (+);
EBVCA-IgG 657 U/ml, EBEA-IgG >150 U/ml;
CD4+ cell count 239, CD8+ cell count 241, NK cell count 37; CD19+ cell count 58; CD45+ 634 (all decreased);
ESR, CRP, PCT, and ferritin all negative;
Fungal D-glucan test: <10 Pg/ml, GM test: 0.15 S/CO (both negative);
Stool Clostridioides difficile (-);
Comprehensive autoimmune panel, rheumatoid factor, anti-CCP, anticardiolipin antibody, and HLA-B27 all showed no abnormalities;
Urine, stool, and blood cultures negative;
Blood mNGS: no pathogenic organisms detected.
Whole-body PET-CT showed multiple nodular and small patchy hyperdense opacities in both lungs with increased metabolism (SUV 2-5.5), with infection considered possible (fungal?); indistinct mesenteric spaces in the abdominal cavity, multiple nodules and small patchy opacities, with increased metabolism (SUV 6.6); focal increased metabolism in the left iliac bone (SUV 3.8), without bone destruction.
Echocardiography: no obvious abnormalities.
